<title>BRAZIL: Brazil to issue new export-boosting measures - paper.</title>
<headline>Brazil to issue new export-boosting measures - paper.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-04-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Brazilian government will announce measures in the coming days to reduce the cost of agricultural exports, local newspapers said on Friday.</p>
<p>Internal Revenues Service Secretary Everardo Maciel told Folha de Sao Paulo newspaper that a government decree, which would probably be issued next week, would allow exporters of frozen meat goods to be refunded for payment of the so-called Cofins and PIS/Pasep taxes.</p>
<p>--Fatima Cristina, Sao Paulo Newsroom 5511 2485412</p>
